class.description:
A [ResourceLoadResult] is returned by [method ResourceLoader.load_result] and [method ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_result]. Unlike [method ResourceLoader.load], which returns [code]null[/code] on failure and only prints the reason, it tells the caller [i]why[/i] a load failed: [member error] is the [enum Error] code and [member error_message] is the message the loader printed. It is read-only after creation.
It is a [RefCounted] and not a struct because the binding layer (GDScript, C#, GDExtension) cannot expose C++ structs; like a value, it is freed automatically when no longer used.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var result := ResourceLoader.load_result("res://levels/level_1.tres", "PackedScene")
if result.ok:
	add_child(result.resource.instantiate())
elif result.error == ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND:
	print("No such level: ", result.path)
else:
	push_error(result.error_message)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
ResourceLoadResult result = ResourceLoader.LoadResult("res://levels/level_1.tres", "PackedScene");
if (result.Ok)
{
    AddChild(((PackedScene)result.Resource).Instantiate());
}
else if (result.Error == Error.FileNotFound)
{
    GD.Print("No such level: ", result.Path);
}
else
{
    GD.PushError(result.ErrorMessage);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
In C#, [code]ResourceLoader.TryLoad<T>(path, out T resource)[/code] and [code]ResourceLoader.TryLoad<T>(path, out T resource, out Error error)[/code] wrap this class in the usual [code]Try[/code] pattern.
